# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command step
usage 1   step | s [<count>]            single-step one CPU instruction (or <count> of them)
usage 2   step over                     run the call at the current instruction to completion, then halt
usage 3   step out                      run until the current routine returns to its caller
usage 4   step <cpu> [<count>|over|out] same, stepping another processor - `cpus` lists them

case instructions, over and out
target fake
covers 1-4
$ step
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
$ s
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step 4
out 26
Stepping 4 instructions...
status 0
action Step { }
$ s 2
out 26
Stepping 2 instructions...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step 0
out 30
Step count must be at least 1.
status 1
action none
$ step x
out 37
'x' is not 'over', 'out', or a count.
status 1
action none
$ step over
out 90
This core does not report a call stack to its breakpoints, so `step over` cannot be armed.
status 1
action none
$ step out
out 56
Already at the outermost frame - nothing to step out of.
status 1
action none
$ step gsu
out 59
gsu cannot be halted by this core, so it cannot be stepped.
status 1
action none
$ step cop 1
out 59
gsu cannot be halted by this core, so it cannot be stepped.
status 1
action none
$ step cpu 2
out 26
Stepping 2 instructions...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step cpu over
out 90
This core does not report a call stack to its breakpoints, so `step over` cannot be armed.
status 1
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1-4
$ step over
out 87
This core does not report a call stack, so `step over` has no depth to measure against.
status 1
action none
$ step out
out 86
This core does not report a call stack, so `step out` has no depth to measure against.
status 1
action none
$ step gsu
out 39
'gsu' is not 'over', 'out', or a count.
status 1
action none
$ step cop
out 42
This cartridge has no coprocessor to step.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ step
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ step
out 58
No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

case other processors on venus-sa1
target venus-sa1
covers 4
$ cpus
out 465
SNES debug processors:
  cpu   PC=$00ED3E  Ricoh 5A22 (65816) main CPU
        supports: bp, cov, bt, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: CpuBus
  spc   PC=$00FFCF  Sony SPC700 sound CPU
        supports: bp, cov, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: APURAM
  sa1   PC=$000000  SA-1 (65816) cartridge coprocessor
        supports: bp, cov, bt, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: SA1BUS
Scope a command by putting the name first, e.g. `bp sa1 add 8000` or `cov gsu on`.
status 0
action none
$ step sa1
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step gsu
out 39
'gsu' is not 'over', 'out', or a count.
status 1
action none
$ step cop
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
end

case other processors on venus-gsu
target venus-gsu
covers 4
$ cpus
out 452
SNES debug processors:
  cpu   PC=$00EA88  Ricoh 5A22 (65816) main CPU
        supports: bp, cov, bt, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: CpuBus
  spc   PC=$00FFCF  Sony SPC700 sound CPU
        supports: bp, cov, regs, setreg, disasm   code space: APURAM
  gsu   PC=$000000  SuperFX GSU cartridge coprocessor
        supports: bp, cov, regs, disasm   code space: GSUBUS
Scope a command by putting the name first, e.g. `bp sa1 add 8000` or `cov gsu on`.
status 0
action none
$ step sa1
out 39
'sa1' is not 'over', 'out', or a count.
status 1
action none
$ step gsu
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step cop
out 27
Stepping one instruction...
status 0
action Step { }
end

case the count is hexadecimal
target fake
covers 1
$ step 10
out 27
Stepping 16 instructions...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step 0x10
out 27
Stepping 16 instructions...
status 0
action Step { }
$ step A
out 27
Stepping 10 instructions...
status 0
action Step { }
end
